research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a8-def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral.log:14452:**Given:** A natural $m \ge 1$, reals $a \le b$, a function $f : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ that is integrable when $a<b$, with components $f_0,\dots,f_{m-1}$, and the vector $v := \int_a^b f \in \mathbb{R}^{m}$; write $g(t) := \sum_{i<m} f_i(t)^{2}$, so that $\lVert f(t)\rVert_2 = \sqrt{g(t)}$ ([[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-p-norms-on-rn]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a8-def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral.log:14454:[L1] The vector-valued integral is componentwise: when $a<b$, $f$ is integrable exactly when every $f_i$ is bounded and Darboux integrable, and then $\bigl(\int_a^b f\bigr)_i = \int_a^b f_i$; $\int_a^a f = 0$ ([[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[def-darboux-integral]], [[def-oriented-integral]], [[def-bounded-set]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a8-def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral.log:14458:[L3] Monotonicity of the integral: for $a<b$ and integrable $u \le w$ on $[a,b]$, $\int_a^b u \le \int_a^b w$; and an integrable $u \ge 0$ has $\int_a^b u \ge 0$ ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a8-def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral.log:14460:[L4] Products and squares: if $u,w$ are integrable on $[a,b]$ then so are $|u|$, $u^{2}$ and $uw$ ([[cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a8-def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral.log:14496:6.2 If $v = 0$ then $\lVert v\rVert_2 = 0$, while $\int_a^b\lVert f\rVert_2 \ge 0$ because $\lVert f\rVert_2 \ge 0$ pointwise and $a<b$; so clause 2 holds in this case. [step 5.1, L3, L8]
